 ### How are Google's departments read?
 
 Google's postings name no department, so the site sorts each Google job title into one of 27 job families named after Google's own careers categories (Software Engineering, Technical Program Management, Data Center Operations and so on); a title it can't read is "No department". It reads 97% of Google's titles, and on a hand-checked sample of 100 postings it put 92 in the right family. The Department filter says "Grouped by job title" on a board whose departments are read this way.
 
+### How are roles compared with other companies?
+
+**Same role elsewhere** and **Compare companies** sort every role into one of 29 job families by its title and, where the title doesn't say, its department: software engineering, data center technicians, warehouse, delivery and store operations, customer support and success, and so on. A role is compared with the same family at the same level in the same country. Amazon's warehouse, delivery-station and store associates, the process assistants and leads of their shifts and the managers who run those sites are their own family, not customer support, so a technical account manager is not compared with a delivery-station associate. On a data-center campus the department decides: an electrical subject matter expert there is data-center work, not an AI tutor.
