 ### Where does a pay estimate come from?
 
-A pay estimate (on jobs with no posted pay, and in Insights) is worked out from the posted pay of the most similar roles at the same company and in the same country, weighted by how close each title and level is. "Typically within ±N%" is how far, in the middle case, the estimate was from the real posted pay when we tested it on postings whose pay we hid. It is an estimate, not a figure from the posting.
+A pay estimate (on jobs with no posted pay, and in Insights) is worked out from the posted pay of the most similar roles at the same company and in the same country, weighted by how close each title and level is. "Typically within ±N%" is how far, in the middle case, the estimate was from the real posted pay when we tested it on postings whose pay we hid. It is an estimate, not a figure from the posting. Insights lists the five most comparable roles. Where more roles are equally similar than that, it shows ones spread across the pay the estimate used (the nearest to its middle, its low end and its high end, then halfway between), from the lowest pay to the highest, so the five show the range the estimate came from rather than the newest postings.
 
